---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import NavBar from '../../components/NavBar.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
---
<Layout title="Research" description="Methodology, kinematics, and Monte Carlo results behind the Face Forward parking simulation.">
  <NavBar />
  <main id="main">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-16 lg:px-8 lg:py-20">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[.22em] text-gold">The Research</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 font-display text-4xl font-semibold sm:text-5xl">Methodology & Findings</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-chalk/70">
        Our position is grounded in a reproducible kinematic simulation, not intuition alone. Below is a summary of
        the model, the Monte Carlo protocol, and where you can read the full technical treatment.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
        <a
          href="/docs/methodology.pdf"
          class="rounded-sm bg-gold px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-forest transition-brand duration-200 hover:brightness-110"
        >
          Download Whitepaper (PDF)
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/hughrscott/face-forward"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
          class="rounded-sm border border-chalk/25 px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-chalk transition-brand duration-200 hover:border-gold hover:text-gold"
        >
          Simulation Source (GitHub)
        </a>
      </div>

      <section class="mt-14 space-y-6">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold">Model summary</h2>
        <div class="grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <div class="card-surface rounded-sm p-6">
            <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[.16em] text-gold">Kinematics</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-chalk/75">
              Non-holonomic Ackermann steering model, 2.8m wheelbase, state vector [x, y, &theta;, v] with
              acceleration and steering-angle control inputs.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="card-surface rounded-sm p-6">
            <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[.16em] text-gold">Line of sight</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-chalk/75">
              Driver eye position 1.2m forward of the rear axle; sightlines blocked by adjacent-vehicle geometric
              shadows (SUV: 2.0m &times; 5.2m &times; 1.9m).
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="card-surface rounded-sm p-6">
            <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[.16em] text-gold">State machine</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-chalk/75">
              Gear-shift delay (1.0s), stochastic driver reaction latency (&mu;=0.75s, &sigma;=0.15s), and a
              0.5s-per-sweep visual scan rate model cognitive and mechanical latency.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="card-surface rounded-sm p-6">
            <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[.16em] text-gold">Monte Carlo protocol</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-chalk/75">
              10,000 randomized trials sweeping pedestrian density (0.05&ndash;0.30 ped/m), aisle width
              (5.5&ndash;7.2m), and adjacent SUV probability (0&ndash;0.8), logging cycle time, proximity warnings,
              critical conflicts, and collisions.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-14">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold">Empirical validation roadmap</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-chalk/70">
          The simulation establishes a theoretical case. The next phase validates it against real-world observation.
        </p>
        <ol class="mt-6 space-y-5">
          <li class="card-surface rounded-sm p-5">
            <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[.16em] text-gold">Phase 1 &middot; Planned</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-chalk/75">
              Camera-based pilot at 2&ndash;3 volunteer parking lots, capturing anonymized top-down footage of
              forward and reverse maneuvers during peak pedestrian hours.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li class="card-surface rounded-sm p-5">
            <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[.16em] text-gold">Phase 2 &middot; Planned</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-chalk/75">
              Automated trajectory extraction and near-miss detection pipeline, calibrated against the simulation's
              collision and proximity thresholds.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li class="card-surface rounded-sm p-5">
            <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[.16em] text-gold">Phase 3 &middot; Not started</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-chalk/75">
              Comparative statistical analysis of observed conflict rates against simulated predictions, published
              as a follow-up whitepaper.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</Layout>
